          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "qsq69dd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "9. ELECTRIC POWER"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mkb0pkz",
      "content": "• Rate of doing electrical work."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lqlx2ca",
      "content": "P = VI"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dpv2yre",
      "content": "Also: P = I²R and P = V²/R"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ktyu4w8",
      "content": "SI unit: Watt (W)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ikizw7j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "10. HEATING EFFECT OF CURRENT (JOULE’S LAW)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vfwaada",
      "content": "Heat produced: H = I²Rt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gkp7nee",
      "content": "Applications: Electric heater, fuse, bulb filament."
    },
    {
      "id": "0pw5l37",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "11. COMMERCIAL UNIT OF ENERGY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t7hm536",
      "content": "1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ Joule"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m7o969l",
      "content": "Electric bill calculated in kWh units."
    },
    {
      "id": "f0y25s1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "12. FUSE AND MCB"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jlkdfy3",
      "content": "• Fuse protects circuit from overcurrent."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "1 kWh is equal to 3.6 × 10⁶ Joules or 1 Commercial Unit of Electricity.",
        "Ammeters are connected in series with ideal zero resistance, while Voltmeters are connected in parallel with ideal infinite resistance.",
        "A fuse wire is always connected in series with the live wire and must have high resistance and a low melting point.",
        "MCBs (Miniature Circuit Breakers) work on the magnetic effect of current, whereas electrical fuses work on the heating effect."
      ],
      "id": "2kg4oli"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qhs58rc",
      "content": "• Made of low melting point alloy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lrecunz",
      "content": "• MCB automatically switches off during overload."
    },
    {
      "id": "bigz4ym",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
